+# Finish the synchronization review
+
+The existing Promote/Upgrade mechanism now cleans up interrupted new-file writes and reports the distinction between working bytes and delivery manifests explicitly.
+This review proposes resolutions and onboarding work; it applies none of the nineteen promotion conflicts.
+Pablo authorized bounded defect fixes and review. Codex acted as ASDG Admin with distribution/synchronization focus and Attitude Off in the existing chat.
+
+![Both directions compare source, baseline and target; human review precedes any apply.](../../../asdg/docs/images/synchronization.svg)
+
+## Actual bounded changes
+
+Rollback now records the device/inode of each exclusively created file, removes its partial contents on failure and preserves a replacement inode.
+Failed stream setup closes the raw descriptor; earlier changes and newly created empty directories roll back. Same-inode concurrent edits and crash recovery remain outside the transaction guarantee.
+New tests first reproduced partial-file and empty-file leaks, then passed after the fix; creation failure and replacement-inode preservation are also covered.
+Previews and adoption records now identify `WORKING_TREE_SNAPSHOT` or `MANIFEST_MATCHED_DISTRIBUTION`, manifest MATCH/STALE, manifest SHA/version and exact added/modified/deleted paths.
+Matching hashes establish content identity only: validation and human approval both remain `NOT_ESTABLISHED`. Upgrade apply still rejects a stale canonical manifest.
+The portable suite passed **117 tests on Python 3.15.0**; all **27 synchronization tests passed on Python 3.9.6**.
+The [technical receipt](02.3-review-synchronization.json) lists exact changed paths, hashes, test evidence, checks and preservation limits.
+
+## Reconciliation evidence and proposal
+
+Source: sibling `speakercoach`, `sprint-00`, HEAD `f0388497ac781e12631dc573b3a300100c056162`, clean; canonical: `main`, HEAD `7c5d0ca3869ca2bf6472ac7a408b809dc4823cf9`, existing uncommitted candidate preserved.
+The source declares `0.2.0-pilot.2`; canonical declares `0.3.0-pilot.1`. Neither label proves which individual change is authoritative.
+All ten present baseline files were recovered from local Git blobs and verified against the shared delivery manifest hashes; nine conflict files were absent in that manifest.
+Review every row in [governance and documentation](02.3.1-conflicts-governance-docs.md) and [runtime and test conflicts](02.3.2-conflicts-runtime-tests.md), with exact three-way diffs linked per file.
+The real dry run remains **0 added, 0 modified, 0 deleted, 395 unchanged, 19 conflicting**; all conflicts still block apply.
+The source delivery manifest is stale: 186 added, 125 modified and 24 deleted paths versus that manifest. These are delivery differences, not proposed promotion actions. This task also changes canonical working bytes while preserving the prior manifest and ZIP; no new distribution was packaged.
+
+## Human review process
+
+1. Review the frozen baseline, source and target hashes and the baseline→source, baseline→target and source→target diffs in the [evidence inventory](../../reviews/asdg-sync-review/conflicts/inventory.json).
+2. Mark each proposed resolution accepted or revised, bound to those hashes. This records a decision, not permission for a bulk overwrite or a human-approved methodology release.
+3. After separate edit authorization, prepare the selected resolutions in an isolated disposable candidate; retain source improvements, canonical fixes and all history. Inspect its resulting diff and run the relevant tests.
+4. Rerun dry-run on that exact candidate. Manual conflict resolution must make source/target agree on accepted results or explicitly decline those source changes; the current CLI has no resolution-file or force flag. Never edit baseline hashes to suppress conflicts.
+5. Rejected/divergent source changes remain visible conflicts; a selective adoption command/receipt is a remaining small gap if future promotion must proceed without reconciling both copies. Do not fabricate successful adoption now.
+6. Authorize any real copy/apply separately against the fresh plan and candidate bytes. Preserve the old manifests and approval bindings; package a newly reviewed version only afterward.
+
+A future selective-resolution option need only bind each keep-target/reviewed-merge choice to baseline, source, target and result hashes, then reuse the existing transaction and adoption receipt. It must not accept an unreviewed force flag; it is proposed, not implemented here.
+
+The governance ledger already contains the complete pilot history: 673 baseline events → 1,379 pilot events → 1,804 canonical events at review start, with exact prefix preservation.
+Retain canonical history and append only new maintenance receipts; this task does not merge, delete, deduplicate or reapprove historical events.
+See [integration refresh](02.3.3-integration-refresh.md) and [ZIP/Clone × Script/Prompt gaps](02.3.4-onboarding-gaps.md) for proposed next work.
+No real promotion, reverse upgrade, lifecycle bypass, hook/trust change, commit, push, merge or publication occurred.
